      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). This order is double that, which raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nThe order may have a typo or a mix-up between per-dose and daily totals. Possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO** at a different frequency\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. If 1700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you verified it, though I'd advise against it. Once you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
