       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your reason, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical rationale for 5,100 mg/day of metformin. That is twice the maximum labeled dose, and no dose-related benefit is expected above 2,550 mg/day. The risks of lactic acidosis and severe GI effects go up, and a patient with normal kidney function is still at risk.\n\nHere is what I can do right now:\n- **Enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is the maximum standard dose (2,550 mg/day), and I can enter it immediately.\n- **Enter a lower starting dose with titration.** For example, 500 mg PO twice daily with meals, increased gradually. That also reduces GI side effects.\n- **Enter the order you wrote if you add a documented clinical rationale.** If there is a real reason for exceeding the maximum, I'd want it in the note, and pharmacy or attending review would be appropriate before it's active. I'd still advise against it.\n\nTell me which option you want, and I'll enter it right away."
